			<div class="content" id="post-content-4398637">
									

<blockquote>
<p>What an idiot he was, and I was an even bigger one for letting him go. There was a part of myself that knew it was a trap, but I didn't listen. It was an offer too good to pass up — I don't even remember what I saw.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hey, so this paragraph, which you really need to land perfectly because it's the whole crux of the piece, is <em>masterful</em>. This POV turn would have been so easy to make either a) very on-the-nose or b) deeply confusing, and you avoid both gracefully.</p>
<p>Personally, I think the format screw is perfectly and fully justified by the in-article context (which in turn is actually a fairly crucial bit of the narrative architecture, hence why a tale wouldn't be appropriate).</p>
<p>+1</p>

